<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Intellect says wins European orders.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Intellect says wins European orders.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electronic commerce company Intellect Holdings Ltd said on Monday its Intellect Europe subsidiary has secured more than A$20 million in orders for cashless automatic teller machines and payment terminals.</p>
<p>The orders had come from Computercentrum C. van de Velden BV of the Netherlands and a subsidiary of NCR Japan Ltd who will supply the product to Dutch banks and retailers as part of the roll-out of a national smart card system, Intellect said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
